https://oxide-and-friends.transistor.fm/episodes/helios

Bryan and Adam are joined by Oxide colleagues Josh Clulow, Patrick Mooney, and Steve Klabnik to discuss Helios, the operating system that runs on the Oxide Rack. Helios is a distro of illumos (derived from OpenSolaris, derived from Solaris, etc.). What's a distro? Why did Oxide choose illumos? Plenty of cross-generational appeal in this episode!

Some of the topics we hit on, in the order that we hit them:

* The Helios github repo
* Hacker News thread its release
* [[OmniOS]]
* Rust Tier 2 support
* Bryan's talk on holistic boot
* Oxide and Friends: Holistic Boot
* Oxide and Friends: Shipping Rack 1
* [[The Quality Death Spiral]]
* Oxide's "St. Louis" branch of illumos
* Bryan's sleeper bug from 1991
* illumos books (How's this for some SEO?!)